Multiply {A} by itself to make {D}. Then {D} is a cube. [!just IX.3]

Since {A} multiplied by itself makes {D}, and multiplied by {B} makes {C}, therefore {A} is to {B} as {D} is to {C}. And, since {A} and {B} are cubic numbers, therefore {A} and {B} are similar solid numbers. Therefore two mean proportional numbers fall between {A} and {B}, so that two mean proportional numbers fall between {D} and {C} also. [!just VII.17; VIII.19; VIII.8]

And {D} is a cube, therefore {C} is also a cube. [!just VIII.23]

Therefore, *if a cubic number multiplied by a cubic number makes some number, then the product is cubic.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide: Of course, *m*<sup>3</sup>*n*<sup>3</sup> = (*mn*)<sup>3</sup>.
